        10:Tc4e,<h1>Import Rules and Regulations</h1><p>Thinking about importing a car from Japan to the United Kingdom? This page covers which cars can be imported, the tests a car needs before it can be registered, how it is shipped, and the duty and VAT charged when it arrives.</p><h2>Which Cars Can Be Imported</h2><h3>Vehicle Age</h3><p>The United Kingdom sets <strong>no age limit</strong> on imported cars. A car's age decides which tests it needs before it can be registered, and whether it can be treated as a collector's item for duty and VAT.</p><h3>Steering Position</h3><p>Both <strong>right-hand drive and left-hand drive</strong> cars can be imported. Most Japanese cars are right-hand drive, the same as cars sold in the UK.</p><h3>Vehicle Type</h3><ul><li><strong>Passenger cars</strong> with up to 9 seats, including the driver's seat.</li><li><strong>Cars under 10 years old</strong> must be unmodified and must have been registered in Japan for at least six months before they are exported. These are the conditions for the IVA test to accept the car's Japanese approval.</li></ul><h2>Tests Before Registration</h2><p>No inspection is needed in Japan before the car ships. In the UK, a car may need one or both of these tests before it can be registered:</p><ul><li><strong>Individual Vehicle Approval (IVA):</strong> for cars under 10 years old, carried out by the Driver and Vehicle Standards Agency (DVSA). Fee: £199.</li><li><strong>MOT:</strong> for cars 3 years old or more. Fee: £54.85. Cars built more than 40 years ago do not need one.</li></ul><h2>Shipping</h2><ul><li><strong>Arrival ports:</strong> Southampton or Bristol (Portbury)</li><li><strong>Shipping method:</strong> RoRo (Roll-on/Roll-off)</li><li><strong>Shipping line:</strong> Höegh Autoliners, sailing monthly</li><li><strong>Time at sea:</strong> 30-50 days</li></ul><h2>Duties and Taxes</h2><p>Duty and VAT are worked out on the <strong>CIF value</strong>: the price of the car plus the sea freight to the UK.</p><ul><li><strong>Customs duty:</strong> 0% for cars made in Japan, and 10% of the CIF value for cars made elsewhere. The 0% rate comes from the UK–Japan trade agreement, and Carbarn's invoice carries the statement of origin it requires.</li><li><strong>Import VAT:</strong> 20% of the CIF value plus customs duty.</li><li><strong>Collector's items:</strong> a car that is 30 years old or more, unmodified, and of a model no longer in production pays 0% customs duty and 5% import VAT.</li></ul><h2>Registration in the United Kingdom</h2><ul><li><strong>Arrival notice (NOVA):</strong> the car's arrival is reported to HM Revenue &amp; Customs within 14 days.</li><li><strong>First registration with the DVLA:</strong> £55.</li><li><strong>Vehicle tax for the first year:</strong> for cars under 10 years old, set by the car's CO2 emissions. For older cars, £230 for engines up to 1,549 cc and £375 above. Cars built more than 40 years ago pay none.</li></ul><p>Duty and VAT are paid to HM Revenue &amp; Customs when the car is cleared. The tests and the DVLA registration are booked by you or your clearing agent once the car has been unloaded.</p>11:T1fda,<h1>Privacy Policy – Carbarn United Kingdom</h1><h2>1. Introduction</h2><p>This Privacy Policy ("Policy") explains how <strong>Carbarn LLC</strong>, a company registered in Japan ("Carbarn", "we", "us" or "our"), collects, uses and protects your personal information when you use this website or our services to import a vehicle from Japan to the United Kingdom.</p><p>By using this website or placing an order, you agree to the practices described in this Policy. Carbarn operates from Japan and does not currently trade through a United Kingdom registered entity.</p><h2>2. What Information We Collect</h2><p>2.1 Personal information. To process a vehicle order and provide export services we may collect:</p><ul><li>Full name</li><li>Contact details (e-mail address, telephone number, delivery address)</li><li>Identity document details where export or customs documentation requires them</li><li>Purchase history and saved vehicle preferences</li><li>How you use this website</li><li>Payment confirmation, received through a secure third-party payment processor</li></ul><p>2.2 Financial information. We accept bank transfer and credit or debit card. We do not store full card details; card payments are handled by our payment processor.</p><h2>3. Why We Use Your Information and On What Basis</h2><p>We use your personal data to:</p><ul><li>Perform our contract with you — processing your order, preparing export and shipping documentation, and supporting you through delivery</li><li>Comply with legal obligations — Japanese export law, and the customs and registration information required at destination</li><li>Pursue our legitimate interests — keeping this website secure, preventing fraud, and improving our service</li><li>Send optional service or marketing updates, where you have consented</li></ul><p>We do not sell your personal information.</p><h2>4. Who We Share Your Information With</h2><ul><li><strong>Shipping lines and logistics partners</strong> — to arrange export and ocean carriage</li><li><strong>Clearing agents and inspection bodies</strong> — where you ask us to pass documentation on</li><li><strong>IT and hosting providers</strong> — to operate this website securely</li><li><strong>Government authorities</strong> — where export, customs or registration law requires it</li><li><strong>Professional advisers</strong> — where we are required to take legal or accounting advice</li><li><strong>Google</strong> — where you have consented, to provide website analytics and advertising measurement (see section 8)</li></ul><h2>5. International Transfers</h2><p>Carbarn operates from Japan, so information you provide is transferred to and processed in Japan, and may be shared with partners in the country of destination in order to complete your shipment. We apply contractual and technical safeguards to those transfers.</p><h2>6. How Long We Keep Your Data</h2><p>We keep order, export and customs records for as long as export, tax and accounting law requires, and we keep enquiry and marketing data only for as long as it remains useful for the purpose it was given.</p><h2>7. Data Security</h2><ul><li>Encrypted connections across the platform</li><li>Access to customer data restricted to staff who need it</li><li>Hosting on secured servers</li><li>No storage of full payment credentials</li></ul><p>We maintain strict security standards, though no transmission of data over the internet can be made entirely secure.</p><h2>8. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2><p>We use cookies and similar technologies on this website. Strictly necessary cookies are always active because the website cannot function without them. All other cookies are optional and are used only if you consent to them, in accordance with the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations (PECR) and the UK GDPR.</p><p><strong>Strictly necessary cookies.</strong> These enable core functions of the website, such as signing in to your account, remembering your chosen currency and keeping the vehicles you have saved.</p><p><strong>Analytics cookies (“Help us improve”).</strong> With your consent, we use Google Analytics, a web analytics service provided by Google, to understand how visitors use our website, including which vehicles, pages and searches are viewed, so that we can improve the website and the vehicles we offer. We do not send your name, telephone number or email address to Google Analytics.</p><p><strong>Advertising cookies (“Ads for cars you’d like”).</strong> With your consent, Google may use information about your visits to our website to show you advertisements for vehicles that may interest you on Google services and other websites, and to help us measure the effectiveness of our advertising.</p><p><strong>Measurement from our systems.</strong> If you have consented to analytics cookies, we may also send Google Analytics a record of certain actions connected with your visit, such as when an enquiry, order or payment is recorded. These records are linked to the pseudonymous identifier that Google Analytics has assigned to your browser and, if you are signed in, to an internal customer reference. They do not include your name or contact details. If you have not consented, no such records are sent.</p><p><strong>Legal basis and your choices.</strong> Our legal basis for using optional cookies, and for the related measurement, is your consent. When you first visit the website you can accept or reject optional cookies, or choose individual categories, and you can change or withdraw your consent at any time by selecting “Cookie settings” at the bottom of any page. Withdrawing your consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before you withdrew it. We remember your choice for six months, after which we will ask you again. You can also block or delete cookies through your browser settings.</p><p><strong>Retention and international transfers.</strong> Google Analytics data is kept for up to 14 months. Google may process this information in the United States and in other countries outside the United Kingdom. Google states that such transfers are protected by appropriate safeguards, including the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and its UK Extension and standard contractual clauses. For more information, please see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google’s Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from websites that use its services</a>.</p><h2>9. Your Rights</h2><p>Under United Kingdom data protection law — the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018 — you have the right to:</p><ul><li>Ask what personal data we hold about you and receive a copy of it</li><li>Have inaccurate data corrected</li><li>Ask us to erase your data where we no longer need it</li><li>Ask us to restrict how we use your data, or object to our using it</li><li>Receive the data you gave us in a portable format, or ask us to transfer it</li><li>Withdraw consent at any time, where we relied on your consent</li><li>Object to direct marketing at any time</li></ul><p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us at info@carbarn.uk. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office, the United Kingdom's data protection regulator.</p><h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2><p>We do not knowingly collect data from anyone under 18. If we become aware that we have, we will delete it.</p><h2>11. External Links</h2><p>This website may link to third-party sites. Carbarn is not responsible for the privacy practices of those sites.</p><h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2><p>We may update this Policy when the law changes, when our services change, or in response to customer feedback. The current version is always the one published on this site.</p><h2>13. Contact</h2><p>Questions about this Policy, or about the personal data we hold, can be sent to info@carbarn.uk. Carbarn LLC is registered and operates in Japan.</p>12:T14eb,<h1>Terms and Conditions – Carbarn United Kingdom</h1><h2>1. Introduction</h2><p>These Terms and Conditions ("Agreement") govern the relationship between you (the "Purchaser") and <strong>Carbarn LLC</strong>, a company registered in Japan ("Carbarn", "we", "us" or "our"), in connection with the purchase and export of used vehicles from Japan to the United Kingdom.</p><p>By using this website and purchasing a vehicle through us, you agree to these terms. Carbarn does not currently trade through a United Kingdom registered entity; the contract of sale is made with Carbarn LLC in Japan.</p><h2>2. Nature of Business</h2><ul><li>Carbarn LLC is a Japan-based exporter of used vehicles, including to the United Kingdom.</li><li>Carbarn sources, owns and exports the vehicles listed on this site.</li><li>All vehicle transactions, ownership transfers and export documentation are processed in Japan.</li><li>Carbarn's shipping responsibility concludes on handover of the vehicle to the shipping line at the port of export in Japan.</li><li>Carbarn does not act as a customs clearing agent in the United Kingdom and does not register vehicles with the licensing authority on your behalf.</li></ul><h2>3. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h2><ul><li>This Agreement is governed by the laws of Japan, and disputes arising from it are to be resolved in the courts of Japan.</li><li>Nothing in this Agreement removes or limits any right you have as a consumer under the mandatory consumer protection law of the United Kingdom.</li></ul><h2>4. Vehicle Condition and Inspection</h2><ul><li>Vehicles are inspected in Japan by Carbarn before listing. The United Kingdom does not require a pre-shipment inspection certificate from Japan.</li><li>Each listing carries photographs, the Carbarn inspection comments, the inspection report and, where the vehicle is bought at auction, the auction sheet and grade.</li><li>Odometer readings are recorded as they appear on the auction sheet and the Japanese export certificate.</li><li>Vehicles are used goods and are sold in their described condition. The condition report and auction sheet form the description you rely on.</li></ul><h2>5. Shipping and Delivery</h2><ul><li>Vehicles are shipped by RoRo (Roll-on/Roll-off) from Japan.</li><li>Destination ports are Southampton and Bristol (Portbury).</li><li>Sailings are monthly and transit is 30–50 days, subject to vessel schedules.</li><li>Sailing dates and arrival dates are set by the carrier and can move. Carbarn is not responsible for carrier delays, port congestion, demurrage or storage charges once a vehicle has been handed to the shipping line.</li></ul><h2>6. Payment Terms</h2><ul><li>A deposit is payable before shipment is arranged; the amount and the due date are stated on your proforma invoice.</li><li>We accept bank transfer and credit or debit card.</li><li>Bank details are issued only on an official Carbarn proforma invoice, after your quote is confirmed.</li><li>Bank charges, intermediary fees and currency conversion costs are the Purchaser's responsibility.</li><li>Shipment is arranged only once the payment stated on the proforma invoice has cleared.</li></ul><h2>7. Customs Clearance and Registration in the United Kingdom</h2><ul><li>The Purchaser is responsible for customs clearance in the United Kingdom and for all duty, tax and clearance costs.</li><li>Duty and VAT are charged by HM Revenue &amp; Customs (HMRC).</li><li>A Notification of Vehicle Arrivals (NOVA) must be filed with HMRC within 14 days of the vehicle arriving.</li><li>Cars aged 3 to 10 years require an Individual Vehicle Approval (IVA) test at registration; cars over 10 years require an MOT.</li><li>First registration is issued by the Driver and Vehicle Licensing Agency (DVLA).</li></ul><p>Documents supplied by Carbarn with the shipment:</p><ul><li>Registration Certificate (Country of Origin)</li><li>Export Certificate</li><li>Original Invoice</li><li>Bill of Lading</li><li>Condition Report</li></ul><h2>8. Cancellation and Refunds</h2><ul><li>An order may be cancelled before the vehicle is handed to the shipping line, subject to deduction of costs already incurred.</li><li>Once a vehicle has been shipped, cancellation is not possible and the sale stands.</li><li>These provisions apply in addition to, and do not displace, any cancellation right you hold as a consumer under United Kingdom law.</li></ul><h2>9. Limitation of Liability</h2><ul><li>Carbarn is not liable for port delays, demurrage or storage charges.</li><li>Carbarn is not liable for the outcome of customs clearance, the approval test or registration, all of which are decided by the relevant authority.</li><li>Carbarn is not liable for loss or damage occurring after the vehicle has been handed to the shipping line.</li><li>Nothing in this section limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited.</li></ul><h2>10. Privacy and Data Protection</h2><ul><li>We collect only the customer data needed to process an order and meet export and customs obligations.</li><li>Customer information is not sold, and is not shared with unauthorised third parties.</li><li>Our Privacy Policy sets out your rights under United Kingdom data protection law in full.</li></ul><h2>11. Contact</h2><p>Questions about this Agreement can be sent to info@carbarn.uk. Operated by Carbarn LLC, Japan.</p>2:["$","html",null,{"lang":"en-GB","className":"__variable_369f12","suppressHydrationWarning":true,"style":"$undefined","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"id":"ga-gtag-init","strategy":"afterInteractive","children":"$e"}],["$","body",null,{"suppressHydrationWarning":true,"className":"font-[family-name:var(--font-manrope)] font-normal antialiased bg-white","children":["$","$Lf",null,{"config":{"id":24,"code":"GB","name":"United Kingdom","flag":"🇬🇧","website":"www.carbarn.uk","inspection":null,"inspectionFee":null,"inspectionFeeCurrency":null,"dutySource":"RULE_SET","maxAge":{"cars":9999,"vans":9999,"trucks":9999},"minAge":{},"ageBasis":null,"arrivalPorts":["Southampton","Bristol (Portbury)"],"shipping":"RORO","currency":"GBP","countryOfOrigin":"Japan","approxArrivalTimeInDays":"30-50","excludedBrands":[],"heroImageUrl":null,"mapImageUrl":null,"heroTitle":"Buy Used Cars from <span class=\"font-bold\">Japan to the UK</span> with Trusted Inspection Reports","googleSiteVerificationId":null,"gaMeasurementId":"G-P484QSZPT2","ga4ApiSecretSet":true,"canonicalHost":"www.carbarn.uk","languageRegion":"en-GB","logoUrl":"https://fastlycb.s3.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/country-config/carbarn-uk-logo (1).png","facebookPageId":null,"officeAddress":null,"officeHours":null,"officeMapEmbedUrl":null,"localEntityName":null,"customsAuthorityNote":"Buyers are responsible for paying all duties and taxes due to HM Revenue & Customs (HMRC). The vehicle is then registered with the Driver and Vehicle Licensing Agency (DVLA), and the test it needs before registration is carried out by the Driver and Vehicle Standards Agency (DVSA).","shippingRouteDescription":"Your vehicle will be shipped from Japan to Southampton or Bristol (Portbury) Port via RoRo (Roll-on/Roll-off) shipping. Once it arrives, you can clear it through your preferred clearing agent, collect it from the port, and file the Notification of Vehicle Arrivals (NOVA) with HM Revenue & Customs within 14 days.","aboutContent":null,"socialMediaLinks":{"facebook":"https://www.facebook.com/carbarnuk","instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/carbarnuk/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/@CarbarnUK"},"dutyPercentages":[{"name":"Import Duty","percentage":10},{"name":"VAT","percentage":20}],"faqs":[{"question":"Are there any hidden costs?","answer":"The listed price covers the vehicle and ocean freight from Japan. Duty, VAT and customs clearance are charged and paid in the United Kingdom and are quoted separately."},{"question":"Do cars over 30 years old pay a different VAT rate?","answer":"Cars aged 30 years or more are charged import VAT at 5% instead of 20%. Import policies can change; confirm the current treatment with HM Revenue & Customs before you commit."},{"question":"Does the car have to be inspected in Japan before it ships?","answer":"No. The United Kingdom requires no inspection in Japan before shipment. The checks happen after arrival: a Notification of Vehicle Arrivals (NOVA) filing within two weeks, then the test set by the car's age."},{"question":"How are vehicles shipped from Japan to the UK?","answer":"Vehicles are shipped by RoRo (Roll-on/Roll-off) with Höegh Autoliners and unloaded at Southampton or Bristol (Portbury)."},{"question":"How do I check the vehicle condition?","answer":"Every listing carries photographs, the Carbarn inspection comments, the full inspection report, and the auction grade, so the condition can be verified before you commit."},{"question":"How is duty and VAT calculated in the UK?","answer":"Customs Duty is 10% of the CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) value, and VAT is 20% of the CIF value plus duty. Import policies can change; check with HM Revenue & Customs (HMRC) for the latest rates."},{"question":"How long does it take for the vehicle to arrive in the UK?","answer":"Shipping from Japan takes 30-50 days, depending on the sailing. Ships depart monthly."},{"question":"What fixed fees apply when the car is registered?","answer":"Cars aged 3 to 10 years pay an Individual Vehicle Approval (IVA) test fee of £325. Driver and Vehicle Licensing Agency (DVLA) first registration is £55."},{"question":"What is the age restriction on imported cars in the UK?","answer":"The United Kingdom has no age limit for cars or vans. Cars aged 3 to 10 years need an Individual Vehicle Approval (IVA) test before registration. Cars over 10 years need only an MOT."},{"question":"What payment methods do you accept?","answer":"Carbarn accepts Bank Transfer and Credit / Debit Card. Bank details are issued only on an official Carbarn proforma invoice, after your quote is confirmed."}],"shippingSchedules":[],"heroDescription":"Every car in Carbarn's own stock is owned and inspected by Carbarn, and auction cars are bought for you when your bid wins, so UK buyers know the condition, the documents and the costs upfront.","importRules":"$10","privecyAndPolicy":"$11","termsAnsConditions":"$12","status":"ACTIVE","shippingIncluded":true,"supportEmail":"info@carbarn.uk","supportPhone":null,"supportWhatsapp":null,"freightRatePerCbmUsd":125,"priceRoundingStep":100,"shippingFrequency":"Monthly","shippingCarrier":"Höegh Autoliners","stockLandedCostEnabled":true,"stockSource":"JP_STOCK","primaryListing":"AUCTION","auctionSettings":{"tier":"BID","depositMode":"STRIPE","landedCost":"DUTY_ENGINE","allowedCategories":["PASSENGER"],"steering":["RHD"],"ban":null,"agentFee":null,"popularCategories":["people-carriers","kei-cars","hybrid","vans-campers","4wd","sports"],"depositRule":{"bands":[{"uptoJpy":1500000,"amountJpy":150000,"percent":null},{"uptoJpy":3000000,"amountJpy":300000,"percent":null},{"uptoJpy":5000000,"amountJpy":500000,"percent":null},{"uptoJpy":8000000,"amountJpy":null,"percent":15},{"uptoJpy":null,"amountJpy":null,"percent":20}],"roundUpTo":500}},"features":{"carSpecsEnabled":false,"carSpecsClosedAs":"GONE","seoTemplatesEnabled":true,"legalComplianceBadge":false,"payAtOfficeEnabled":false,"cardPaymentsEnabled":true,"taxFactsEnabled":true,"localCurrencyFirst":true,"combinedProductLayout":false,"proseLayer":true,"homepageComposition":false,"homepageSections":[],"heroFacts":[],"requireDutyToList":false,"searchIndexing":true,"searchPages":{"home":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"auctionHome":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"auctionCategories":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":"CHOSEN","chosen":["people-carriers","kei-cars","hybrid","vans-campers"],"withoutStock":null},"auctionMakes":{"index":false,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"auctionModels":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":"CHOSEN","chosen":["suzuki/jimny","toyota/land-cruiser","toyota/prius","mazda/bongo","nissan/elgrand","nissan/skyline","toyota/alphard","toyota/hiace","honda/acty-truck","suzuki/carrytrack","honda/beat","mitsubishi/pajero","nissan/silvia","toyota/estima","honda/stepwgn"],"withoutStock":null},"auctionModelCodes":{"index":false,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"auctionLots":{"index":false,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"stockHome":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"stockModels":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":false},"stockCars":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":nu